<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herod of Chalcis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/48">48 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Herod V</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herod of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Agrippa I</a>. In 41 CE the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> made him king of Chalcis in the Beqaa valley, and later gave him authority over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Temple in Jerusalem</a> and the right to appoint its high priests. He married his niece Berenice. After his death in 48 his kingdom passed to his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agrippa-ii">Agrippa II</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herod-of-chalcis.jpg" alt="Herod of Chalcis" width="320" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Herod_of_Chalcis_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
